# --- Cross-package test seams (EU1001 by design) ----------------------------
# Exported for exactly one consumer that CANNOT reach an unexported form,
# because it lives in another package. The export is the contract.
#   RoutePatterns (wirespec) — the exception table for the bidirectional
#     route-table drift guard in server/wirespec_consistency_test.go:16,94. The
#     data must live in wirespec (the endpoint SSOT) and the guard must live in
#     server (where registerRoutes is), so the export is structurally forced.
#   SecretKeyNames (confighandlers) — sole consumer is root-package
#     providers_test.go:137, which cross-checks every `Secret: true`
#     provider-schema field against the redaction list. confighandlers cannot
#     import the root package.
#   ResetPreserving (authstore) — the destructive-auth-migration seam. Named by
#     boltstore/migrations.go:18 and migrate.go:48 in prose and exercised
#     end-to-end from boltstore/migrate_reset_test.go:496.
#   Suite (store/storetest and authstore/authstoretest) — engine-agnostic
#     contract suites; a suite in the engine's own package could not stay
#     engine-agnostic. One consumer each: boltstore/contract_test.go:22 and
#     authstore/contract_test.go:90.
#   CookieNameSecure (authhandlers) — the "__Host-" name is produced at runtime
#     by the auth library's PosturePerRequest cookie config; this constant is
#     the independent expected side of that contract, referenced 14 times across
#     4 test files in 2 packages (server: auth_login, auth_integration,
#     auth_setup; authhandlers: cookie_test). Its sibling CookieNameHTTP is
#     production-live, so only the HTTPS half looks unused.
function RoutePatterns
function SecretKeyNames
function ResetPreserving
function Suite
constant CookieNameSecure

